    n->item = get_item_from_tag(name);
```
Reason:
The logic incorrectly checks for the existence of a tag for the node name "__root__". If the tag does not exist, it could lead to errors when trying to create the root node, as it would not handle the special case for "__root__" correctly.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (!strcmp(name, "__root__"))
    n->item = list_first_entry_or_null(&menu.master, struct item, master);
else
    n->item = get_item_from_tag(name);
```
Reason:
The new logic explicitly checks if the node name is "__root__" and assigns the root node correctly from the master list, thus preventing issues related to tag existence checks for this specific name. This ensures that the root node is created without errors.

